# Trivy ignore file for both container scans: the PR-side per-platform scan
# in lgtm-ci reusable-docker and the post-merge `vulnerability-scan` job in
# .github/workflows/docker-build-publish.yml. Plain format on purpose: Trivy
# loads ./.trivyignore from the checkout root by default, and the reusable
# workflow has no ignore-file input.
#
# Every entry is time-boxed with its own `exp:` date and its own reason
# comment for its own blocker. Do NOT batch-assign a shared expiry date
# across unrelated advisories (same rule as .osv-scanner.toml). Once `exp:`
# passes, Trivy reports the finding again and the scan fails, which forces
# a re-check of the blocker.

# DSA-6572-1: ca-certificates 20250419 in the gcr.io/distroless/static:nonroot
# runtime base (docker/Dockerfile). Debian ships the fix as 20250419+deb13u1
# in trixie-security, but no distroless static:nonroot build has picked it up
# yet: the current index
# sha256:516757106de35205efb70b91ba03f6f1298424a0678c603255cf2852a7000087
# still ships 20250419. Remove this entry when a distroless digest with
# 20250419+deb13u1 lands (Renovate digest bump of docker/Dockerfile).
# Re-verified 2026-10-21 (#1059).
DSA-6572-1 exp:2026-11-21
